<h2>Head &amp; Spinal Injuries — บาดเจ็บที่ศีรษะและกระดูกสันหลัง</h2>
<blockquote>"Spinal injury ทำให้พิการได้ตลอดชีวิต — immobilize ให้ถูกต้อง"</blockquote>
<h3>Head Trauma (TBI — Traumatic Brain Injury)</h3>
<h4>ภาพรวม</h4>
<p>TBI แบ่งตาม severity:</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Severity</th><th>GCS</th><th>หมายเหตุ</th></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Mild</strong></td><td>13-15</td><td>Concussion</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Moderate</strong></td><td>9-12</td><td>อาจต้อง surgery</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Severe</strong></td><td>3-8</td><td>ต้อง ICU, intubation</td></tr>
</table>
<h4>GCS (Glasgow Coma Scale)</h4>
<table>
<tr><th>Response</th><th>Score</th></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Eye opening (E)</strong></td><td></td></tr>
<tr><td>Spontaneous</td><td>4</td></tr>
<tr><td>To voice</td><td>3</td></tr>
<tr><td>To pain</td><td>2</td></tr>
<tr><td>None</td><td>1</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Verbal (V)</strong></td><td></td></tr>
<tr><td>Oriented</td><td>5</td></tr>
<tr><td>Confused</td><td>4</td></tr>
<tr><td>Inappropriate words</td><td>3</td></tr>
<tr><td>Incomprehensible sounds</td><td>2</td></tr>
<tr><td>None</td><td>1</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Motor (M)</strong></td><td></td></tr>
<tr><td>Obeys commands</td><td>6</td></tr>
<tr><td>Localizes pain</td><td>5</td></tr>
<tr><td>Withdraws from pain</td><td>4</td></tr>
<tr><td>Flexion (decorticate)</td><td>3</td></tr>
<tr><td>Extension (decerebrate)</td><td>2</td></tr>
<tr><td>None</td><td>1</td></tr>
</table>
<p><strong>⚠️ GCS ≤8 = Intubate!</strong> (cannot protect airway)</p>
<h4>Types of Head Injuries</h4>
<h5>Skull Fracture</h5>
<ul><li><strong>Linear:</strong> รอยร้าว — ไม่ต้อง surgery นอกจาก depressed</li><li><strong>Depressed:</strong> กระดูกยุบ → ต้อง surgery ถ้า &gt;1 cm หรือ over sinus</li><li><strong>Basilar:</strong> ฐานกะโหลก — <strong>Battle's sign</strong> (ecchymosis behind ear) + <strong>Raccoon eyes</strong> (periorbital ecchymosis) + CSF otorrhea/rhinorrhea</li><li><strong>Open:</strong> ผิวหนังฉีก → infection risk</li></ul>
<h5>Concussion (สมองสั่น)</h5>
<ul><li><strong>Mild TBI</strong> — transient neurological dysfunction</li><li><strong>Symptoms:</strong> Confusion, amnesia (retrograde/anterograde), headache, nausea, dizziness</li><li><strong>No structural damage</strong> on CT</li><li><strong>Management:</strong> Observation, rest, gradual return to activity</li><li><strong>Second impact syndrome:</strong> ถ้ากระแทกซ้ำก่อนหาย → cerebral edema รุนแรง → death</li></ul>
<h5>Epidural Hematoma (EDH) ⭐</h5>
<ul><li><strong>Location:</strong> ระหว่าง skull → dura mater</li><li><strong>Source:</strong> Middle meningeal artery (arterial bleed)</li><li><strong>Classic:</strong> Lucid interval — หมดสติ → ตื่นดี → หมดสติอีก</li><li><strong>CT:</strong> Lens-shaped (biconvex) hematoma</li><li><strong>Treatment:</strong> <strong>Emergency craniotomy</strong> — mortality สูงถ้าไม่ผ่าตัด</li><li><strong>Prognosis:</strong> ดีถ้า operate ทัน (&lt;2 ชม.)</li></ul>
<h5>Subdural Hematoma (SDH) ⭐</h5>
<ul><li><strong>Location:</strong> ระหว่าง dura → arachnoid</li><li><strong>Source:</strong> Bridging veins (venous bleed)</li><li><strong>CT:</strong> Crescent-shaped (concavo-convex) hematoma</li><li><strong>Types:</strong></li><li><strong>Acute:</strong> &lt;72 ชม. — อาการรุนแรง, mortality สูง</li><li><strong>Subacute:</strong> 3-7 วัน</li><li><strong>Chronic:</strong> &gt;3 สัปดาห์ — พบใน elderly/alcoholics, minor trauma ก็เกิด</li><li><strong>Treatment:</strong> Craniotomy (acute), Burr hole (chronic)</li></ul>
<h5>Subarachnoid Hemorrhage (SAH)</h5>
<ul><li><strong>Location:</strong> Subarachnoid space</li><li><strong>Source:</strong> Aneurysm rupture (berry aneurysm) หรือ trauma</li><li><strong>Classic:</strong> "Worst headache of my life" (thunderclap headache)</li><li><strong>CT:</strong> Blood in subarachnoid space, cisterns</li><li><strong>Complications:</strong> Vasospasm (day 3-14), hydrocephalus</li><li><strong>Treatment:</strong> Nimodipine (prevent vasospasm), surgery/coiling</li></ul>
<h5>Intracerebral Hemorrhage (ICH)</h5>
<ul><li><strong>Location:</strong> Within brain parenchyma</li><li><strong>Source:</strong> HTN (most common), amyloid angiopathy, trauma</li><li><strong>Treatment:</strong> BP control, surgery ถ้า large</li></ul>
<h5>Diffuse Axonal Injury (DAI)</h5>
<ul><li><strong>Mechanism:</strong> Deceleration/rotation → shearing of axons</li><li><strong>CT:</strong> อาจปกติหรือเห็น small hemorrhages</li><li><strong>Prognosis:</strong> แย่ — prolonged coma, disability</li></ul>
<h4>Cushing's Reflex (Triad) — ⚠️ Late Sign of ↑ICP</h4>
<p>1. <strong>Hypertension</strong> (SBP ↑)</p>
<p>2. <strong>Bradycardia</strong> (HR ↓)</p>
<p>3. <strong>Irregular breathing</strong> (Cheyne-Stokes, ataxic)</p>
<p><strong>Cushing's reflex = สมองกำลัง herniate!</strong> → ฉุกเฉินสูงสุด</p>
<h4>Herniation Syndromes</h4>
<table>
<tr><th>Type</th><th>Mechanism</th><th>Signs</th></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Uncal (tentorial)</strong></td><td>Temporal lobe → through tentorium</td><td>Ipsilateral pupil dilation (CN III palsy), contralateral hemiparesis</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Subfalcine</strong></td><td>Cingulate gyrus → under falx</td><td>Leg weakness (ACA territory)</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Tonsillar</strong></td><td>Cerebellar tonsils → foramen magnum</td><td>Cardiac arrest, respiratory arrest</td></tr>
</table>
<h4>Management of Severe TBI (Prehospital)</h4>
<p>1. <strong>Intubate</strong> if GCS ≤8 — protect airway</p>
<p>2. <strong>Hyperventilate</strong> (brief, target PaCO2 30-35) ถ้า signs of herniation — ลด cerebral blood volume</p>
<p>3. <strong>Maintain SBP &gt;100</strong> (avoid hypotension → cerebral ischemia)</p>
<p>4. <strong>Head elevation 30°</strong> — ลด ICP</p>
<p>5. <strong>Avoid hypoxia</strong> (SpO2 &gt;94%)</p>
<p>6. <strong>Rapid transport</strong> to trauma center with neurosurgery</p>
<p>7. <strong>Mannitol/Hypertonic saline</strong> ถ้า herniation signs (ALS)</p>
<h3>Spinal Injuries</h3>
<h4>Anatomy Review</h4>
<pre class="code"><code>Cervical: C1-C7 (8 cervical nerves)
Thoracic: T1-T12
Lumbar: L1-L5
Sacral: S1-S5
Coccyx: 1</code></pre>
<h4>Spinal Cord Injury Patterns</h4>
<h5>Complete Spinal Cord Injury</h5>
<ul><li><strong>Complete loss</strong> of motor + sensory below injury level</li><li><strong>Spinal shock:</strong> Flaccid paralysis, areflexia, loss of bowel/bladder (first 24-72 ชม.)</li><li><strong>Prognosis:</strong> Poor — unlikely to recover</li></ul>
<h5>Incomplete Spinal Cord Injury Syndromes</h5>
<table>
<tr><th>Syndrome</th><th>Mechanism</th><th>Motor</th><th>Sensory</th></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Central cord</strong></td><td>Hyperextension (elderly)</td><td>Upper &gt; Lower weakness</td><td>Variable</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Brown-Séquard</strong></td><td>Hemisection</td><td>Ipsilateral weakness</td><td>Ipsilateral proprioception loss, contralateral pain/temp loss</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Anterior cord</strong></td><td>Anterior artery occlusion</td><td>Bilateral weakness</td><td>Pain/temp loss, preserved proprioception</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Posterior cord</strong></td><td>Rare</td><td>Preserved</td><td>Proprioception/vibration loss</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Cauda equina</strong></td><td>Nerve root compression (L2 below)</td><td>Flaccid, asymmetric</td><td>Saddle anesthesia, bowel/bladder dysfunction</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Conus medullaris</strong></td><td>Conus (L1-L2)</td><td>Mixed UMN/LMN</td><td>Saddle, bowel/bladder</td></tr>
</table>
<h5>Neurogenic Shock ⚠️</h5>
<ul><li><strong>Spinal cord injury above T6</strong> → loss of sympathetic tone</li><li><strong>Triad:</strong> Hypotension + Bradycardia + Warm/dry skin (vasodilation)</li><li><strong>Differentiate from hypovolemic shock:</strong> HR ↓ (neurogenic) vs HR ↑ (hypovolemic)</li><li><strong>Treatment:</strong> IV fluid + Vasopressors (Norepinephrine) + Atropine (bradycardia)</li></ul>
<h4>Spinal Immobilization</h4>
<h5>Indications (NEXUS Criteria — ถ้าไม่มีข้อใดข้อหนึ่ง = ไม่ต้อง immobilize)</h5>
<p>1. No midline cervical tenderness</p>
<p>2. No focal neurological deficit</p>
<p>3. Normal alertness (GCS 15)</p>
<p>4. No intoxication</p>
<p>5. No painful distracting injury</p>
<h5>Canadian C-Spine Rule</h5>
<ul><li><strong>High risk</strong> (must image): Age ≥65, dangerous mechanism, paresthesias</li><li><strong>Low risk</strong> (can assess ROM): Simple rear-end MVA, sitting in ER, ambulatory, delayed neck pain, no midline tenderness</li><li><strong>Can rotate 45° both ways</strong> → no imaging needed</li></ul>
<h5>Immobilization Technique</h5>
<p>1. <strong>Manual in-line stabilization (MILS)</strong> — คนหนึ่งถอดศีรษะคงที่ตลอด</p>
<p>2. <strong>Cervical collar</strong> — วัดขนาดให้ถูก (fingerbreadths)</p>
<p>3. <strong>Long spine board</strong> — สำหรับ extrication (ไม่ควรนาน &gt;30 นาที — pressure sores)</p>
<p>4. <strong>Head blocks</strong> — 2 ข้างศีรษะ + tape across forehead</p>
<p>5. <strong>Log roll</strong> — ทีม 3-4 คน, spine ตรงตลอด</p>
<h5>⚠️ Spinal Board Pitfalls</h5>
<ul><li><strong>ห้างนาน &gt;30 นาที</strong> — pressure sores, respiratory compromise, pain</li><li><strong>ใช้สำหรับ extrication เท่านั้น</strong> — ไม่ใช่ transport device</li><li><strong>Vacuum mattress</strong> ดีกว่าสำหรับ transport</li></ul>
<h4>Special Spinal Injuries</h4>
<h5>C1-C2 (Atlas/Axis) Fracture</h5>
<ul><li><strong>Hangman's fracture:</strong> C2 bilateral pars fracture (hyperextension)</li><li><strong>Jefferson's fracture:</strong> C1 burst (axial load)</li><li><strong>Odontoid fracture:</strong> C2 dens fracture — Type II = unstable</li></ul>
<h5>Cervical Facet Dislocation</h5>
<ul><li><strong>Unilateral:</strong> &lt;25% vertebral body displacement</li><li><strong>Bilateral:</strong> 50% displacement — unstable, cord compression</li></ul>
<h5>Thoracolumbar Fracture</h5>
<ul><li><strong>Compression fracture:</strong> Wedge-shaped (osteoporosis, elderly)</li><li><strong>Burst fracture:</strong> Axial load → bone fragments → cord compression</li><li><strong>Chance fracture:</strong> Seatbelt injury — horizontal split (flexion-distraction)</li><li><strong>Fracture-dislocation:</strong> Most unstable — surgery required</li></ul>
<h3>Quiz</h3>
<p><strong>Q1:</strong> Epidural hematoma classic presentation คืออะไร?</p>
<p><strong>A1:</strong> <strong>Lucid interval</strong> — หมดสติ → ตื่นดี → หมดสติอีก (arterial bleed → rapid expansion)</p>
<p><strong>Q2:</strong> Cushing's triad มีอะไรบ้าง?</p>
<p><strong>A2:</strong> <strong>Hypertension + Bradycardia + Irregular breathing</strong> = ↑ICP → herniation</p>
<p><strong>Q3:</strong> Neurogenic shock vs Hypovolemic shock ต่างกันอย่างไร?</p>
<p><strong>A3:</strong> Neurogenic = <strong>Hypotension + Bradycardia + Warm skin</strong>; Hypovolemic = <strong>Hypotension + Tachycardia + Cool skin</strong></p>
<h3>ภาษาไทย: Head/Spinal Injury สำหรับ EMT</h3>
<ul><li><strong>GCS ≤8 = Intubate</strong></li><li><strong>Cushing's triad = herniation</strong> → ส่งเร็วสุด</li><li><strong>Spinal immobilize</strong> ตาม NEXUS criteria</li><li><strong>Neurogenic shock = Bradycardia + Hypotension</strong> (ไม่ใช่ tachycardia!)</li><li><strong>Log roll</strong> — spine ตรงตลอด, ทีม 3-4 คน</li></ul>
